# Delivery and receipt family - executable coverage pins
#
# Run just this suite:
#   ./verify.sh --only new-book-plans/delivery-receipt.pins.nibli
#
# These pins prove two different things and the difference matters. The first
# section proves the routes are DORMANT: the shipped record holds no arrival, so
# no floor actuality derives for anybody through this family. The rest prove the
# routes are not blind — supply the evidence in a probe and the actuality
# derives, strip any one conjunct and it stops. Dormant is not the same as
# absent, and a suite that only showed FALSE could not tell them apart.
#
# Nothing here establishes that anything arrived. Every probe fact below is
# written by this file, not by the world.
:expect-pins 28

# ── The routes ship dormant ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Adam is confined, so shelter and recorded speech derive for him through the
# carceral routes that already existed. Food, care, security and company do not
# derive for anyone at all, and that is the delivery gap this family makes
# representable without closing.
? eats(Adam).
# => FALSE
? healthy(Adam).
# => FALSE
? secure(Adam).
# => FALSE
? meets(Adam).
# => FALSE

# Bela is not confined. Shelter still does not reach her, because the new route
# is dormant and the old one runs through confinement.
? dwell(Bela).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-190 food delivery on recipient-side receipt ───────────────────────
# FS-CCE-190 counterfactual: with the arrival record and an independent
# attestation, food derives; the same person without them derives nothing.
receives(Ama, Meal, Canteen).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Ama).
observe(Inspector, Meal, Ama, FoodScope).
? eats(Ama).
# => TRUE

# FS-CCE-190 negative: an arrival record with no attestation at all feeds
# nothing. The record of a thing changing hands is not evidence it arrived.
receives(Bram, Meal, Canteen).
? eats(Bram).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-191 shelter delivery on recipient-side receipt ────────────────────
# FS-CCE-191 counterfactual: shelter now has a route that does not run through
# a conviction. Cass is not confined and is housed.
receives(Cass, Room, Housing).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Cass).
observe(Inspector, Room, Cass, ShelterScope).
? dwell(Cass).
# => TRUE
? prisoner(Cass).
# => FALSE

# FS-CCE-191 negative: the attestation names a different scope, so the shelter
# route does not fire. A witness cannot certify a nearby fact and have it count.
receives(Dov, Room, Housing).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Dov).
observe(Inspector, Room, Dov, FoodScope).
? dwell(Dov).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-192 care delivery on recipient-side receipt ───────────────────────
# FS-CCE-192 counterfactual: care reaching a person derives the floor item the
# book glosses as being cared for when ill. It does NOT derive that Elia is
# well, and no rule anywhere reads this conclusion as a health finding.
receives(Elia, Treatment, Clinic).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Elia).
observe(Inspector, Treatment, Elia, CareScope).
? healthy(Elia).
# => TRUE

# FS-CCE-192 negative: an attestation with no arrival record behind it certifies
# nothing. This is the shape a provider's own paperwork would take.
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Fen).
observe(Inspector, Treatment, Fen, CareScope).
? healthy(Fen).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-193 material security on recipient-side receipt ───────────────────
# FS-CCE-193 counterfactual: the security floor item derives on the same shape.
receives(Gita, Kit, Depot).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Gita).
observe(Inspector, Kit, Gita, SecurityScope).
? secure(Gita).
# => TRUE

# FS-CCE-193 negative: one route does not leak into another. Gita's security
# arrival says nothing about whether she ate.
? eats(Gita).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-194 company on recipient-side receipt ─────────────────────────────
# FS-CCE-194 counterfactual: company is a floor item and reaches a person the
# same way. The isolation marker reads this conclusion, so it is the one route
# here that an existing alarm can already see.
receives(Hux, Visit, Community).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Hux).
observe(Inspector, Visit, Hux, CompanyScope).
? meets(Hux).
# => TRUE

# FS-CCE-194 negative: an unwitnessed visit derives no company.
receives(Ines, Visit, Community).
? meets(Ines).
# => FALSE

# ── FS-CCE-195 a provider may not certify its own delivery ───────────────────
# This is the family's load-bearing guard and the reason it exists. Jae has an
# arrival record and an attestation, and the attesting witness is the provider
# named as the source. Nothing derives.
# FS-CCE-195 negative: the provider attests its own delivery and it counts for
# nothing.
receives(Jae, Meal, Kitchen).
authorized(Kitchen, DeliveryWitness, Jae).
observe(Kitchen, Meal, Jae, FoodScope).
? eats(Jae).
# => FALSE

# FS-CCE-195 counterfactual: the same evidence with a witness who is not the
# source derives. The only thing that changed is who attested.
receives(Kip, Meal, Kitchen).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Kip).
observe(Inspector, Meal, Kip, FoodScope).
? eats(Kip).
# => TRUE

# ── FS-CCE-196 authorised independent delivery writer ────────────────────────
# FS-CCE-196 negative: a witness who observes but holds no authorised role for
# this person attests nothing. Anyone may watch; not everyone may write.
receives(Liv, Meal, Canteen).
observe(Inspector, Meal, Liv, FoodScope).
? eats(Liv).
# => FALSE

# FS-CCE-196 counterfactual: authorisation is per person, so a role held for
# somebody else does not carry. Mira has a witness authorised for Liv.
receives(Mira, Meal, Canteen).
authorized(Warden, DeliveryWitness, Liv).
observe(Warden, Meal, Mira, FoodScope).
? eats(Mira).
# => FALSE

# A predeclared alternate is another holder of the same authorised role, not a
# second rule. Nyx's ordinary witness is absent and the alternate carries it.
receives(Nyx, Meal, Canteen).
authorized(AlternateWriter, DeliveryWitness, Nyx).
observe(AlternateWriter, Meal, Nyx, FoodScope).
? eats(Nyx).
# => TRUE

# ── FS-CCE-197 an arrival is not conditioned on a roster entry ───────────────
# FS-CCE-197 counterfactual: serve first. A person never entered on the roster,
# whose arrival is independently witnessed, still derives the actuality — and is
# still not on the roster. Requiring personhood here would make the record a
# precondition of being fed.
receives(Oke, Meal, Canteen).
authorized(Inspector, DeliveryWitness, Oke).
observe(Inspector, Meal, Oke, FoodScope).
? eats(Oke).
# => TRUE
? person(Oke).
# => FALSE

# FS-CCE-197 negative: the absence of a roster entry is not a finding either. It
# does not derive that Oke was refused, only that nothing was recorded.
? err(Oke, Undelivered).
# => FALSE

# ── What none of this establishes ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every arrival above was written by this file. The design cannot make one
# happen, and the floor items with no probe stay exactly where they were.
? eats(Bela).
# => FALSE
? healthy(Bela).
# => FALSE
? secure(Bela).
# => FALSE
? meets(Bela).
# => FALSE
